<Base title="About" description="Where the stories, prayers and quotations on He Still Answers come from.">
  <article class="narrow ab">
    <p class="kicker">About</p>
    <h1>True stories of answered prayer</h1>
    <p>In 1885 a book called <em>The Wonders of Prayer</em> gathered hundreds of accounts of answered prayer, sent in by pastors, missionaries, sea captains, widows and children. Many of the writers gave their names and towns. Most of the stories on this site are quoted word for word from that book. A few accounts, and the shorter illustrations from the <em>New Cyclopaedia of Prose Illustrations</em> (1875), are still given in a careful modern retelling. Nothing is added to what the sources say.</p>
    <p>Beside them are the prayers of Charles Haddon Spurgeon (1834–1892), quoted word for word, and lines from Matthew Henry's <em>A Method for Prayer</em> (1710), with the page they appear on.</p>
    <p>All of these books are in the public domain. Every post names its source, so you can read the original for yourself.</p>
  </article>
</Base>
